  m_Name: Ksenia
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SuspectData
  FirstName: Ksenia
  LastName: Darnik
  Nickname: 
  Occupation: Student
  CharacterDescription: "Quiet, wide-eyed, and speaks in a soft, airy voice. She
    has a habit of staring at the player\u2019s chin or hands rather than their eyes. "
  CharacterArc: Her arc is about regression. As the world becomes more terrifying,
    she retreats into a state of infantile simplicity, eventually treating the apocalypse
    like a game of pretend that has gone on too long.
  DateOfBirth: 12/06/1981
  Sex: Female
  EntryPermitExpiryDate: 08 OCT
  IsResident: 1
  GivesPaperwork: 1
  handwritingFont: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f8e89ead54f8523428cc2e34f005bb5e, type: 2}
  startingInfectionScore: 0
  dailyInfectionProgression: 5
  IDPhoto: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 8f8385f1646f13f4293e3177d00b5fa0, type: 3}
  CharacterPrefab: {fileID: 5692054325713852150, guid: 152c7a3af09b2704097391328df986eb, type: 3}
  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Returning home after primary school.
    - Resident returning with family members.
    - Retrieving a lost toy from the park.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Escaping the high radiation zones.
    - Checking on the status of my classroom.
    - Seeking shelter from the black rain.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Seeking refuge from the falling ash.
    - Returning to assigned bunk for safety.
    - Fulfilling mandatory youth census.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Going to work.
    - Returning home to see a pet that died last year.
    - Buying candy from a store that is boarded up.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Looking for a teacher who moved away in 1988.
    - Meeting a friend at the abandoned quarry.
    - Going to work.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Going home to have tea with the shadows.
    - I need to go back and find my missing face.
    - To wait for the monsters to finish their dinner.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Hello. My mom said I have to show you this paper.
    - "It\u2019s very loud out there. Is it always going to be this loud?"
    - I found a shiny stone in the dirt. Do you want to see?
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - Why is your shadow so much longer than you are, mister?
    - "The playground is empty. The swings move even when there\u2019s no wind."
    - "I can hear the buildings whispering. They\u2019re cold and they want blankets."
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - "I\u2019m playing hide and seek with the sun. I think I won."
    - "My dolls told me it\u2019s time to go into the big sleep."
    - Is it tomorrow yet? Or is today just going to stay forever?
  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - "Thank you. I\u2019m going to go see my mom now."
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - Don't let the bad air touch you, mister. It bites.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - "I\u2019m going home to close my eyes. It\u2019s prettier that way."
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
    lastVerdict: 2
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Is this a time-out? I didn't do anything wrong.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - What? Mom will be mad at me if I'm late for dinner!
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - "I\u2019ll just wait here until the world finishes breaking."
  exitDialoguesKilled:
    lastVerdict: 3
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - I just... I just want to go home!
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "It\u2019s getting very dark. I want to go home now."
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Is the game over? I don't want to play anymore.
  quarantineExitLines:
  - "Am I in trouble? I didn\u2019t break anything. I don\u2019t think I broke anything."
  - "It\u2019s just like my corner at home. Except colder."
  - "I\u2019ll be very quiet. I\u2019m good at being quiet. I\u2019ve been practicing."
  killExitLines:
  - "I didn\u2019t do anything wrong\u2026 I was just standing here\u2026"
  - "Is someone going to tell my mom? Can someone\u2026 tell my mom?"
  - "It\u2019s getting very dark\u2026 and I just\u2026 I just want to go home now\u2026"
  voiceAudioClips: []
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The hospital. I work there. Worked there.
    midDaysAnswer: I was checking on a patient who couldn't come in.
    finalDaysAnswer: The hospital. It's not what it used to be.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: School. We had morning lessons today. The teacher let
      us do finger painting.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Home. I don't know if the hospital is still there. I haven't
      checked.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: The playground. I was looking for the other children.
      The swings were empty but I waited.
  - question: Have you been experiencing any strange symptoms lately?
    earlyDaysAnswer: I'm exhausted. That's not unusual for this job though.
    midDaysAnswer: I've had a low fever for two weeks. I know what that means. I'm
      fine.
    finalDaysAnswer: I try not to think about it. There are more pressing things.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: I feel really good! I slept for a very long time. I
      don't remember falling asleep.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: No fever. I checked this morning with my thermometer. Completely
      normal. I feel fine.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: I feel light. Really light. Like if I ran fast enough
      I might not come back down.
  - question: Who do you live with?
    earlyDaysAnswer: Two other nurses. We share the apartment near the hospital.
    midDaysAnswer: One nurse now. The other transferred to the eastern facility.
    finalDaysAnswer: Alone since last week. I don't mind the quiet.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: My mom. She makes my breakfast and braids my hair. She
      is very good at braids.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Both nurses still. Nothing has changed at the apartment.
      Nobody transferred anywhere.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Two nurses. We share the apartment. Everything is the
      same as always. We had dinner together.
  IDNumber: 2549407
